% Test cases for the oral anticancer drugs policy (oral_anticancer.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of Policy Article A52479 and
% per payment condition of LCD L33826, each stating only what its record
% shows. The diagnosis is a code of the article's ICD-10 table. The queries:
% whether the claim is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads its
% checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and what minimal
% change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base oral anticancer cases includes these resources:
    oral_anticancer.

the knowledge base oral anticancer cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a month of capecitabine (J8520) for colon cancer
% (C18.9, group 2): every criterion and every documentation requirement in
% the record.
scenario capecitabine_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the capecitabine.
    the HCPCS code of the capecitabine is "J8520".
    the capecitabine is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "C18.9".
    the capecitabine is approved by the FDA.
    the capecitabine is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    the order for the capecitabine is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the capecitabine is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the capecitabine includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the capecitabine includes order date.
    the order for the capecitabine includes description of the item.
    the order for the capecitabine includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the capecitabine includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the capecitabine was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the capecitabine was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the capecitabine.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Busulfan (J8510) for colon cancer (C18.9): not an indication of its
% injectable form (group 1) — not reasonable and necessary; the same
% busulfan for chronic myeloid leukemia (C92.10) is.
scenario indication_by_group is:
    claim 1 is for the busulfan.
    the HCPCS code of the busulfan is "J8510".
    the busulfan is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "C18.9".
    the busulfan is approved by the FDA.
    the busulfan is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    claim 2 is for the other busulfan.
    the HCPCS code of the other busulfan is "J8510".
    the other busulfan is furnished to Cy.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "C92.10".
    the other busulfan is approved by the FDA.
    the other busulfan is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Methotrexate (J8610) prescribed for immunosuppression in rheumatoid
% arthritis: criterion 3 is not met. A temozolomide (J8700) for a
% glioblastoma (C71.0) prescribed by a practitioner not licensed to
% prescribe anticancer agents: criterion 4 fails.
scenario immunosuppression_and_prescriber is:
    claim 1 is for the methotrexate.
    the HCPCS code of the methotrexate is "J8610".
    the methotrexate is furnished to Dee.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "C50.911".
    the methotrexate is approved by the FDA.
    the methotrexate is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    the methotrexate is prescribed for immunosuppression.
    claim 2 is for the temozolomide.
    the HCPCS code of the temozolomide is "J8700".
    the temozolomide is furnished to Eve.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "C71.0".
    the temozolomide is approved by the FDA.
    rn expects answers [].

% A drug of no code of its own, dispensed as J8999: the record says it is
% topotecan, for ovarian cancer (C56.1, group 8) — covered.
scenario not_otherwise_classified is:
    claim 1 is for the new formulation.
    the HCPCS code of the new formulation is "J8999".
    the new formulation is furnished to Fay.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the drug dispensed as the new formulation is topotecan.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "C56.1".
    the new formulation is approved by the FDA.
    the new formulation is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The antiemetic (J8597) taken one hour before the capecitabine, with the
% practitioner's finding that the drug is likely to induce emesis, is
% covered; the one taken four hours before is not.
scenario antiemetic_timing is:
    claim 1 is for the ondansetron.
    the HCPCS code of the ondansetron is "J8597".
    the ondansetron is furnished to Ann.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the ondansetron is used in conjunction with the capecitabine.
    the ondansetron is administered 1 hours before the oral anticancer drug.
    claim 2 is for the early ondansetron.
    the HCPCS code of the early ondansetron is "J8597".
    the early ondansetron is furnished to Ann.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the early ondansetron is used in conjunction with the capecitabine.
    the early ondansetron is administered 4 hours before the oral anticancer drug.
    the HCPCS code of the capecitabine is "J8520".
    the capecitabine is furnished to Ann.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "C18.9".
    the capecitabine is approved by the FDA.
    the capecitabine is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    the finding anticancer drug likely to induce emesis about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "vomiting within the hour on the first two cycles".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A refill of the monthly capecitabine, affirmed five days before the
% current supply ends and delivered two days before, with continued need and
% use in the record: payable.
scenario capecitabine_refill is:
    claim 1 is for the capecitabine.
    the HCPCS code of the capecitabine is "J8520".
    the capecitabine is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-30.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "C18.9".
    the capecitabine is approved by the FDA.
    the capecitabine is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    the current supply of the capecitabine is expected to end on 2026-06-01.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the capecitabine on 2026-05-27.
    the medical record documents continued need for the capecitabine on 2026-04-10.
    the record documents continued use of the capecitabine on 2026-04-10.
    the order for the capecitabine is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the capecitabine is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the capecitabine includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the capecitabine includes order date.
    the order for the capecitabine includes description of the item.
    the order for the capecitabine includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the capecitabine includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the capecitabine was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the capecitabine was delivered on 2026-05-30.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the capecitabine.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The antiemetic claim whose narrative names everything but the frequency of
% administration: reasonable and necessary, but the article's documentation
% is missing — payable fails at the remedy.
scenario antiemetic_narrative_incomplete is:
    claim 1 is for the ondansetron.
    the HCPCS code of the ondansetron is "J8597".
    the ondansetron is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the ondansetron is used in conjunction with the capecitabine.
    the ondansetron is administered 1 hours before the oral anticancer drug.
    the claim narrative for the ondansetron identifies drug name.
    the claim narrative for the ondansetron identifies manufacturer.
    the claim narrative for the ondansetron identifies dosage strength.
    the claim narrative for the ondansetron identifies oral anticancer drug used.
    the HCPCS code of the capecitabine is "J8520".
    the capecitabine is furnished to Ann.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "C18.9".
    the capecitabine is approved by the FDA.
    the capecitabine is prescribed by a practitioner licensed under state law to prescribe anticancer chemotherapeutic agents.
    the finding anticancer drug likely to induce emesis about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the ondansetron is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the ondansetron is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the ondansetron includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the ondansetron includes order date.
    the order for the ondansetron includes description of the item.
    the order for the ondansetron includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the ondansetron includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the ondansetron was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the ondansetron was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the ondansetron.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the claim narrative for the ondansetron identifies frequency of administration"]].

